 ## Audit
 
 The build fails on: an unknown status or a missing grid cell; a TeX error; any reference to another
 host (no fonts, scripts, styles or images are fetched; a Content-Security-Policy forbids it); a broken
 in-page link or duplicate id; and reader-visible words that name tools or models, files, internal
-identifiers or workflow (the mathematics-only rule for reader-facing text).
+identifiers, workflow or process stages, or give percentages (the mathematics-only rule for
+reader-facing text). The same rule covers words inside formulas (`\text{}`), the attributes a reader
+hears or sees (aria-label, title, alt, placeholder, page metadata) and element ids; raw TeX delimiters
+in reader text or TeX in an attribute also fail. Warnings, which do not block, list words that may be
+workflow residue for the content writer to read, formulas written outside TeX delimiters, and
+statements without an `id` (no link reaches them).
